          "excerpt": "BOSNIAN FOREIGN MINISTER SACIRBEY CALLED ON AMBASSADOR HUNTER MID-DAY JULY 12. BASED ONA TELEPHONE CONVERSATION WITH PRESIDENT IZETBEGOVIC EARLIER IN THE DAY, SACIRBEY SAID THAT THE GOVERNMENT'S PRIMARY CONCERN WAS THE WELFARE OF THE PEOPLE IN SERBRENICA. HE SPECULATED THE SERBS WERE INTENT ON PICKING OFF THE ENCLAVES ONE-BY-ONE, ATTEMPTING TO RE-WRITE THE CONTACT GROUP MAP BY GRABBING 4 TO 5 PERCENT MORE TERRITORY. HE EXPRESSED CONFIDENCE ABOUT THE ABILITY OF THE ENCLAVES -- INCLUDING ZEPA -- TO HOLD OFF SERB ATTACKS. HE EXPRESSED NO DOUBTS ABOUT GORAZDE, IN PARTICULAR. WITH RESPECT TO ZEPA, HE NOTED THAT THE FIGHTERS THERE HAD A GOOD REPUTATION AND WOULD FIGHT FIERCELY, BUT ADMITTED THERE …",
